{"id":"ca3139e842d84130ec9ed39bdfaa57ee3998bd1d","axis":"silent","repo":"argoproj/argo-cd","sha":"ca3139e842d84130ec9ed39bdfaa57ee3998bd1d","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/operator-manual/argocd-secret.yaml","lines":["@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@ data:","   webhook.azuredevops.username: shhhh! it's an azure devops secret","   # azure devops webhook password","   webhook.azuredevops.password: shhhh! it's an azure devops secret","+  # harbor webhook secret","+  webhook.harbor.secret: shhhh! it's a harbor secret"," ","   # an additional user password and its last modified time (see user definition in argocd-cm.yaml)","   accounts.alice.password:"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/operator-manual/webhook.md","lines":["@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@ provider's webhook secret configured in step 1."," | Gogs            | `webhook.gogs.secret`            |"," | Azure DevOps    | `webhook.azuredevops.username`   |"," |                 | `webhook.azuredevops.password`   |","+| Harbor          | `webhook.harbor.secret`          |"," "," Edit the Argo CD Kubernetes secret:"," ","@@ -211,6 +212,77 @@ For example, these `repoURL` values all match a webhook event for `ghcr.io/myorg"," - `oci://GHCR.IO/MyOrg/MyImage`"," - `oci://ghcr.io/myorg/myimage/`"," ","+### Harbor","+","+[Harbor](https://goharbor.io/) is a CNCF open-source OCI-compliant registry that supports sending webhook events when artifacts are pushed. Argo CD can be configured to receive these events and instantly refresh applications backed by OCI artifacts stored in Harbor.","+","+> [!NOTE]","+> Harbor does not send a distinctive request header to identify webhook events, unlike GitHub which sends `X-GitHub-Event`.","+> Authentication is performed via a configurable **Authorization** header value that you set in both Harbor's webhook","+> configuration and in the ArgoCD secret. Configuring the secret (`webhook.harbor.secret`) is **required** for Harbor webhook support.","+","+> [!WARNING]","+> Harbor's Authorization header is a static bearer token, which is weaker than HMAC-based signing used by GitHub/GitLab.","+> Unlike HMAC, a captured token can be replayed indefinitely and does not provide payload integrity guarantees.","+> To reduce risk:","+>","+> - **Always use HTTPS** between Harbor and Argo CD so the token cannot be intercepted in transit.","+> - **Use a strong, randomly generated secret** (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).","+> - **Rotate the secret periodically** by updating both `webhook.harbor.secret` in `argocd-secret` and the Auth Header in Harbor's webhook configuration.","+> - **Restrict network access** to the `/api/webhook` endpoint at the network/firewall level so only your Harbor instance can reach it.","+","+#### Configure the Webhook Secret","+","+In `argocd-secret`, set the Harbor webhook secret. This value must match the **Auth Header** you configure in Harbor's webhook settings:","+","+```yaml","+apiVersion: v1","+kind: Secret","+metadata:","+  name: argocd-secret","+  namespace: argocd","+type: Opaque","+stringData:","+  webhook.harbor.secret: <your-harbor-auth-header-value>","+```","+","+#### Configure the Webhook in Harbor","+","+1. Log in to the Harbor portal with project administrator privileges.","+2. Navigate to your **Project** → **Webhooks** → **Add Webhook**.","+3. Select notify type **HTTP**.","+4. Select payload format **Default**.","+5. Enable the **Artifact pushed** event type.","+6. Set **Endpoint URL** to `https://<argocd-server>/api/webhook`.","+7. Set **Auth Header** to the same value you configured in `webhook.harbor.secret`.","+8. Click **Add** to save the webhook.","+","+> [!NOTE]","+> Argo CD only acts on `PUSH_ARTIFACT` events (artifact push). Other events such as `PULL_ARTIFACT`,","+> `DELETE_ARTIFACT`, and scan events are ignored. Push events for resources that have no tag","+> (digest-only pushes) are also ignored.","+","+#### Example Application","+","+When an OCI artifact is pushed to Harbor, Argo CD refreshes Applications with a matching `repoURL`:","+","+```yaml","+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1","+kind: Application","+metadata:","+  name: my-app","+spec:","+  source:","+    repoURL: oci://harbor.example.com/myproject","+    targetRevision: v1.0.0","+    chart: mychart","+  destination:","+    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc","+    namespace: default","+```","+","+The `targetRevision` field supports exact tags as well as semver constraints (e.g. `^1.0.0`, `>=1.2.0`). See the [GHCR semver constraint table](#example-application) for details and examples.","+"," ## Application Annotations Used by Webhooks"," "," A webhook event triggers a refresh by setting the `argocd.argoproj.io/refresh` annotation on each matching"],"additions":72,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"server/server.go","lines":["@@ -816,6 +816,7 @@ func (server *ArgoCDServer) watchSettings() {"," \tprevBitbucketUUID := server.settings.GetWebhookBitbucketUUID()"," \tprevBitbucketServerSecret := server.settings.GetWebhookBitbucketServerSecret()"," \tprevGogsSecret := server.settings.GetWebhookGogsSecret()","+\tprevHarborSecret := server.settings.GetWebhookHarborSecret()"," \tprevExtConfig := server.settings.ExtensionConfig"," \tvar prevCert, prevCertKey string"," \tif server.settings.Certificate != nil && !server.Insecure {","@@ -867,6 +868,10 @@ func (server *ArgoCDServer) watchSettings() {"," \t\t\tlog.Infof(\"gogs secret modified. restarting\")"," \t\t\tbreak"," \t\t}","+\t\tif prevHarborSecret != server.settings.GetWebhookHarborSecret() {","+\t\t\tlog.Infof(\"harbor secret modified. restarting\")","+\t\t\tbreak","+\t\t}"," \t\tif !reflect.DeepEqual(prevExtConfig, server.settings.ExtensionConfig) {"," \t\t\tprevExtConfig = server.settings.ExtensionConfig"," \t\t\tlog.Infof(\"extensions configs modified. Updating proxy registry...\")"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"util/settings/settings.go","lines":["@@ -118,6 +118,8 @@ type ArgoCDSettings struct {"," \tWebhookBitbucketServerSecret string `json:\"webhookBitbucketServerSecret,omitempty\"`"," \t// WebhookGogsSecret holds the shared secret for authenticating Gogs webhook events"," \tWebhookGogsSecret string `json:\"webhookGogsSecret,omitempty\"`","+\t// WebhookHarborSecret holds the shared secret for authenticating Harbor webhook events","+\tWebhookHarborSecret string `json:\"webhookHarborSecret,omitempty\"`"," \t// WebhookAzureDevOpsUsername holds the username for authenticating Azure DevOps webhook events"," \tWebhookAzureDevOpsUsername string `json:\"webhookAzureDevOpsUsername,omitempty\"`"," \t// WebhookAzureDevOpsPassword holds the password for authenticating Azure DevOps webhook events","@@ -463,6 +465,8 @@ const ("," \tsettingsWebhookBitbucketServerSecretKey = \"webhook.bitbucketserver.secret\""," \t// settingsWebhookGogsSecret is the key for Gogs webhook secret"," \tsettingsWebhookGogsSecretKey = \"webhook.gogs.secret\"","+\t// settingsWebhookHarborSecret is the key for Harbor webhook secret","+\tsettingsWebhookHarborSecretKey = \"webhook.harbor.secret\""," \t// settingsWebhookAzureDevOpsUsernameKey is the key for Azure DevOps webhook username"," \tsettingsWebhookAzureDevOpsUsernameKey = \"webhook.azuredevops.username\""," \t// settingsWebhookAzureDevOpsPasswordKey is the key for Azure DevOps webhook password","@@ -1842,6 +1846,7 @@ func (mgr *SettingsManager) updateSettingsFromSecret(settings *ArgoCDSettings, a"," \tsettings.WebhookBitbucketUUID = string(argoCDSecret.Data[settingsWebhookBitbucketUUIDKey])"," \tsettings.WebhookBitbucketServerSecret = string(argoCDSecret.Data[settingsWebhookBitbucketServerSecretKey])"," \tsettings.WebhookGogsSecret = string(argoCDSecret.Data[settingsWebhookGogsSecretKey])","+\tsettings.WebhookHarborSecret = string(argoCDSecret.Data[settingsWebhookHarborSecretKey])"," \tsettings.WebhookAzureDevOpsUsername = string(argoCDSecret.Data[settingsWebhookAzureDevOpsUsernameKey])"," \tsettings.WebhookAzureDevOpsPassword = string(argoCDSecret.Data[settingsWebhookAzureDevOpsPasswordKey])"," ","@@ -2090,6 +2095,11 @@ func (a *ArgoCDSettings) GetWebhookGogsSecret() string {"," \treturn ReplaceStringSecret(a.WebhookGogsSecret, a.Secrets)"," }"," ","+// GetWebhookHarborSecret returns the resolved Harbor webhook secret","+func (a *ArgoCDSettings) GetWebhookHarborSecret() string {","+\treturn ReplaceStringSecret(a.WebhookHarborSecret, a.Secrets)","+}","+"," // GetWebhookAzureDevOpsUsername returns the resolved Azure DevOps webhook username"," func (a *ArgoCDSettings) GetWebhookAzureDevOpsUsername() string {"," \treturn ReplaceStringSecret(a.WebhookAzureDevOpsUsername, a.Secrets)"],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"util/webhook/harbor.go","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@","+package webhook","+","+import (","+\t\"crypto/subtle\"","+\t\"encoding/json\"","+\t\"errors\"","+\t\"fmt\"","+\t\"io\"","+\t\"net/http\"","+\t\"net/url\"","+\t\"strings\"","+","+\tlog \"github.com/sirupsen/logrus\"","+","+\t\"github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/v3/common\"","+)","+","+const (","+\t// harborEventPushArtifact is the Harbor webhook event type for artifact push.","+\tharborEventPushArtifact = \"PUSH_ARTIFACT\"","+)","+","+// HarborPayload represents the Default format payload sent by Harbor webhooks (Harbor 2.x).","+// See https://goharbor.io/docs/2.12.0/working-with-projects/project-configuration/configure-webhooks/","+type HarborPayload struct {","+\t// Type is the event type, e.g. \"PUSH_ARTIFACT\", \"PULL_ARTIFACT\", \"DELETE_ARTIFACT\".","+\tType      string          `json:\"type\"`","+\tOccurAt   int64           `json:\"occur_at\"`","+\tOperator  string          `json:\"operator\"`","+\tEventData HarborEventData `json:\"event_data\"`","+}","+","+// HarborEventData holds the resources and repository information from a Harbor webhook event.","+type HarborEventData struct {","+\tResources  []HarborResource `json:\"resources\"`","+\tRepository HarborRepository `json:\"repository\"`","+}","+","+// HarborResource describes a single artifact resource within a Harbor webhook event.","+type HarborResource struct {","+\tDigest      string `json:\"digest\"`","+\tTag         string `json:\"tag\"`","+\tResourceURL string `json:\"resource_url\"`","+}","+","+// HarborRepository describes the repository associated with a Harbor webhook event.","+type HarborRepository struct {","+\tName         string `json:\"name\"`","+\tNamespace    string `json:\"namespace\"`","+\tRepoFullName string `json:\"repo_full_name\"`","+\tRepoType     string `json:\"repo_type\"`","+\tDateCreated  int64  `json:\"date_created\"`","+}","+","+// harborParser parses Harbor registry webhook requests and implements Extractor.","+//","+// Harbor does not provide a standard signature header; instead it supports a","+// configurable Authorization header value that the operator sets in both Harbor's","+// webhook configuration and in the ArgoCD secret as webhook.harbor.secret.","+// Configuring the secret is required — an empty secret disables Harbor webhook","+// support entirely to prevent unauthenticated triggering.","+type harborParser struct {","+\tsecret string","+}","+","+// newHarborParser constructs a new harborParser with the given pre-shared secret.","+// When secret is empty the parser will refuse all requests via CanHandle.","+func newHarborParser(secret string) *harborParser {","+\treturn &harborParser{secret: secret}","+}","+","+// CanHandle returns true when the request carries the configured Harbor Authorization","+// header value. If no secret is configured this always returns false, disabling Harbor","+// webhook support.","+func (p *harborParser) CanHandle(r *http.Request) bool {","+\tif p.secret == \"\" {","+\t\treturn false","+\t}","+\tgot := r.Header.Get(\"Authorization\")","+\tif got == \"\" {","+\t\treturn false","+\t}","+\tif subtle.ConstantTimeCompare([]byte(got), []byte(p.secret)) == 1 {","+\t\treturn true","+\t}","+\tlog.WithField(common.SecurityField, common.SecurityHigh).Info(\"Harbor webhook auth header mismatch\")","+\treturn false","+}","+","+// Parse reads the request body, validates that it is a Harbor push event,","+// and returns the corresponding *RegistryEvent.","+// Returns (nil, nil) for non-push events (e.g. pull, delete, scan).","+func (p *harborParser) Parse(r *http.Request) (any, error) {","+\tbody, err := io.ReadAll(r.Body)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"harbor webhook: failed to read request body: %w\", err)","+\t}","+","+\tvar payload HarborPayload","+\tif err := json.Unmarshal(body, &payload); err != nil {","+\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"harbor webhook: failed to parse payload: %w\", err)","+\t}","+","+\tif payload.Type != harborEventPushArtifact {","+\t\treturn nil, nil","+\t}","+","+\t// Find the first resource that carries a tag (digest-only pushes are skipped).","+\tfor _, resource := range payload.EventData.Resources {","+\t\tif resource.Tag == \"\" || resource.ResourceURL == \"\" {","+\t\t\tcontinue","+\t\t}","+\t\tregistryURL, err := parseHarborRegistryURL(resource.ResourceURL)","+\t\tif err != nil {","+\t\t\tlog.Warnf(\"harbor webhook: skipping resource with unparseable resource_url %q: %v\", resource.ResourceURL, err)","+\t\t\tcontinue","+\t\t}","+\t\trepository := payload.EventData.Repository.RepoFullName","+\t\tif repository == \"\" {","+\t\t\t// Fall back to constructing namespace/name if repo_full_name is absent.","+\t\t\tns := payload.EventData.Repository.Namespace","+\t\t\tname := payload.EventData.Repository.Name","+\t\t\tif ns == \"\" || name == \"\" {","+\t\t\t\treturn nil, errors.New(\"harbor webhook: repository name cannot be determined (repo_full_name, namespace, and name are all empty)\")","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\trepository = ns + \"/\" + name","+\t\t}","+\t\treturn &RegistryEvent{","+\t\t\tRegistryURL: registryURL,","+\t\t\tRepository:  repository,","+\t\t\tTag:         resource.Tag,","+\t\t}, nil","+\t}","+","+\treturn nil, nil","+}","+","+// parseHarborRegistryURL extracts the registry hostname from a Harbor resource URL.","+// resource_url format: \"<hostname>/<namespace>/<repo>:<tag>\" or \"<hostname>/<namespace>/<repo>@<digest>\"","+func parseHarborRegistryURL(resourceURL string) (string, error) {","+\trawURL := resourceURL","+\tif !strings.Contains(resourceURL, \"://\") {","+\t\trawURL = \"oci://\" + resourceURL","+\t}","+","+\tparsed, err := url.Parse(rawURL)","+\tif err != nil || parsed.Host == \"\" || parsed.Path == \"\" || parsed.Path == \"/\" {","+\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"harbor webhook: cannot parse registry hostname from resource_url %q\", resourceURL)","+\t}","+\treturn parsed.Host, nil","+}"],"additions":151,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"util/webhook/harbor_test.go","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,280 @@","+package webhook","+","+import (","+\t\"net/http/httptest\"","+\t\"strings\"","+\t\"testing\"","+","+\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\"","+\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"","+)","+","+const testHarborSecret = \"my-harbor-secret\"","+","+func TestHarborParser_CanHandle(t *testing.T) {","+\ttests := []struct {","+\t\tname       string","+\t\tsecret     string","+\t\tauthHeader string","+\t\twant       bool","+\t}{","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:       \"matching secret\",","+\t\t\tsecret:     testHarborSecret,","+\t\t\tauthHeader: testHarborSecret,","+\t\t\twant:       true,","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:       \"wrong secret\",","+\t\t\tsecret:     testHarborSecret,","+\t\t\tauthHeader: \"wrong-secret\",","+\t\t\twant:       false,","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:       \"empty auth header\",","+\t\t\tsecret:     testHarborSecret,","+\t\t\tauthHeader: \"\",","+\t\t\twant:       false,","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:       \"no secret configured\",","+\t\t\tsecret:     \"\",","+\t\t\tauthHeader: testHarborSecret,","+\t\t\twant:       false,","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:   \"no secret configured, no auth header\",","+\t\t\tsecret: \"\",","+\t\t\twant:   false,","+\t\t},","+\t}","+","+\tfor _, tt := range tests {","+\t\tt.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\t\tparser := newHarborParser(tt.secret)","+\t\t\treq := httptest.NewRequestWithContext(t.Context(), \"POST\", \"/api/webhook\",","+\t\t\t\tstrings.NewReader(\"{}\"))","+\t\t\tif tt.authHeader != \"\" {","+\t\t\t\treq.Header.Set(\"Authorization\", tt.authHeader)","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\tassert.Equal(t, tt.want, parser.CanHandle(req))","+\t\t})","+\t}","+}","+","+func TestHarborParser_Parse(t *testing.T) {","+\ttests := []struct {","+\t\tname       string","+\t\tbody       string","+\t\texpectErr  bool","+\t\texpectSkip bool","+\t\texpected   *RegistryEvent","+\t}{","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"valid push artifact event\",","+\t\t\tbody: `{","+\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"PUSH_ARTIFACT\",","+\t\t\t\t\"occur_at\": 1680501893,","+\t\t\t\t\"operator\": \"admin\",","+\t\t\t\t\"event_data\": {","+\t\t\t\t\t\"resources\": [","+\t\t\t\t\t\t{","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"digest\": \"sha256:abc123\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"tag\": \"v1.2.3\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"resource_url\": \"harbor.example.com/myproject/mychart:v1.2.3\"","+\t\t\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\t\t],","+\t\t\t\t\t\"repository\": {","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"mychart\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\"namespace\": \"myproject\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\"repo_full_name\": \"myproject/mychart\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\"repo_type\": \"private\"","+\t\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t}`,","+\t\t\texpected: &RegistryEvent{","+\t\t\t\tRegistryURL: \"harbor.example.com\",","+\t\t\t\tRepository:  \"myproject/mychart\",","+\t\t\t\tTag:         \"v1.2.3\",","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"non-push event is skipped\",","+\t\t\tbody: `{","+\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"PULL_ARTIFACT\",","+\t\t\t\t\"occur_at\": 1680501893,","+\t\t\t\t\"operator\": \"admin\",","+\t\t\t\t\"event_data\": {","+\t\t\t\t\t\"resources\": [","+\t\t\t\t\t\t{","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"digest\": \"sha256:abc123\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"tag\": \"v1.0.0\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"resource_url\": \"harbor.example.com/project/chart:v1.0.0\"","+\t\t\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\t\t],","+\t\t\t\t\t\"repository\": {","+\t\t\t\t\t\